Note about non-linearity: for pskb_may_pull to actually reallocate, the requested length must exceed current linear length (skb_headlen). For receive-path skbs from Ethernet, the header is typically in the linear part; e.g., GRO or fraglist skbs may have short linear area. In the seed (phonet), the packet comes from a socket/datagram path. For our purposes, remote reachability + attacker-controlled length that can exceed headlen (e.g., pulling payload from frags) is enough for a hypothesis.

